new file mode 100644
index 000000000..5a33d1619
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/check-context-v1.schema.json
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+{
+  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
+  "title": "Sail check-only context, version 1",
+  "type": "object",
+  "additionalProperties": false,
+  "required": ["version", "target", "includePaths", "variables", "generatedFiles"],
+  "properties": {
+    "version": {"const": 1},
+    "target": {"type": ["string", "null"]},
+    "includePaths": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute host filesystem path"}},
+    "variables": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {"type": ["boolean", "string"]}},
+    "generatedFiles": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute physical source path"}}
+  },
+  "$comment": "All object keys must be unique. Paths must be absolute according to the compiler host's filename rules; the parser enforces this platform-specific constraint."
+}
diff --git a/doc/check-context.md b/doc/check-context.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..57d78be55
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/check-context.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Check-only context interface (proposal, version 1)
+
+This optional CLI interface lets editor clients reproduce preprocessing and
+project evaluation without selecting a code-generation backend. It is a local
+proposal, not a statement that an official Sail release includes the interface.
+
+`--check-context-version` prints `1` and exits before loading any sources.
+Clients must probe the compiler they will invoke. A client supporting only v1
+must not send a v1 context to a compiler advertising a different version.
+Unsupported options or versions must remain visible to the user; running an
+approximate configuration would make compiler diagnostics misleading.
+
+`--check-context '<JSON>'` accepts the object described by
+[the schema](check-context-v1.schema.json). All five fields are required. The
+parser rejects duplicate keys, unknown fields, unsupported versions, invalid
+value types, and relative filesystem paths before changing compiler state.
+String variables retain their contents, including whitespace and strings that
+spell boolean values. Include paths retain their order. Virtual source aliases
+point to physical files, so their includes and errors retain physical origins.
+File-relative includes take precedence over fallback include paths.
+
+The context implies check-only mode. `target` controls `$iftarget` preprocessing;
+it does not run a code generator. Existing `--project`, root-module selection,
+and ordinary checker options still apply. This interface does not change which
+modules the compiler typechecks before filtering selected output roots.
+
+Build and validate from a checkout with the proposal applied:
+
+```sh
+dune build --release src/bin/sail.exe
+SAIL_UNIT_TESTS=true dune runtest --release test/unit
+_build/default/src/bin/sail.exe --check-context-version
+```
+
+The pure `Check_context` module owns schema validation; the CLI adapter applies
+only a fully parsed context. This keeps the interface testable independently of
+command-line option ordering and limits the compiler entry-point patch.
